Helper policy: helper mask active (bandit/UCB); kept 41/49 prunable helpers (top_k=12, all 39 untried kept, only tried-and-worse helpers pruned)
Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Deep diagnosis: 4% accuracy, 100% syntax, only 2 unique valid molecules out of 50.
// The core problem is that the LM is generating essentially the same 1-2 molecules
// every single run. The repetition penalty on `generated` tokens doesn't help because
// each call starts fresh - `generated` only contains tokens from THIS generation,
// not from previous runs.
//
// The ScaleAllLogits approach failed because that helper isn't in the allowed set.
// Similarly SafePenalizeTokenLogits and SafeBoostTokenLogits are not in the allowed set.
//
// Looking at the ACTUAL allowed helpers:
// - SafeBoostedConstrainedStep: boost specific tokens during constrained generation
// - SafePenalizedConstrainedStep: penalize specific tokens during constrained generation  
// - SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep: penalize tokens already in `generated`
// - GroupBoostedConstrainedStep: boost groups of tokens
// - BoostTokenLogits / PenalizeTokenLogits: direct logit edits (require in-vocab tokens)
//
// The key insight I've been missing: The model generates the SAME molecule because
// with temperature=0 (greedy), it always picks the highest logit token, which is
// always the same. The `generated` sequence in each run is fresh, so repetition
// penalty on `generated` can only penalize tokens already chosen THIS run.
//
// Strategy: Use a MULTI-ATTEMPT approach within the budget.
// 1. Try to generate a molecule, then check if it resembles prompt examples.
// 2. If it's too similar to examples, ROLLBACK and try again with stronger penalties
//    on the first token that was chosen.
// 3. Use PenalizeTokenLogits on the most common first tokens ("O", "N", "C", "S")
//    in alternating patterns across attempts to force diversity.
//
// Better yet: Use the TopValidCandidates + PenalizeTokenLogits approach:
// - Get the top candidates for the first token
// - Penalize the TOP candidate heavily to force the model to pick second/third choices
// - This is the most direct way to get diversity across runs
//
// Implementation:
// 1. Use TopValidCandidates to find what the model would normally pick first
// 2. Heavily penalize that top choice to force an alternative
// 3. Then use SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep for the rest
// 4. Multiple short attempts with rollback if needed
//
// Also: Use BoostTokenLogits/PenalizeTokenLogits (which work on vocabulary tokens)
// to directly manipulate the distribution BEFORE constrained steps.
//
// Critical: After AppendTaskGuidance, the guidance string is appended to the prompt
// permanently. It's first-call-wins. The guidance text itself can heavily bias the
// model toward diversity by listing many different structural templates and asking
// for random selection.
//
// The real issue might be simpler: The model (Qwen3.5-9B) with a SMILES parser
// and greedy decoding will ALWAYS generate the same molecule. We need temperature.
// The only way to get temperature with these tools is through logit manipulation.
//
// New approach: Use BoostTokenLogits/PenalizeTokenLogits to manipulate individual
// logits. After calling TopValidCandidates (which calls GenerateLogits), we can
// manipulate the logits and then use ConstrainedStep (which calls GenerateLogits again).
// Wait - each helper that calls GenerateLogits will re-compute logits fresh from the LM.
// So BoostTokenLogits before ConstrainedStep: the ConstrainedStep will regenerate logits.
//
// Key: BoostTokenLogits and PenalizeTokenLogits are meant to be called AFTER
// GenerateLogits but BEFORE ChooseNextToken. Looking at the Safe* variants:
// SafeBoostedConstrainedStep and SafePenalizedConstrainedStep do: 
//   GenerateLogits -> Penalize/Boost -> Mask -> ChooseNextToken
// These are the right tools!
//
// So: SafePenalizedConstrainedStep(lm, parser, prompt, current, tokensToPenalize, amount, eos)
// will penalize specific tokens. If I penalize "O" at the start, the model won't start with O.
//
// PLAN:
// 1. Use TopValidCandidates to find what the top token would be (costs 1 step)
// 2. Use SafePenalizedConstrainedStep to penalize that top token (forces second choice)
// 3. Continue with SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep
//
// But this still doesn't help between runs - each run the top token is the same.
// 
// The REAL solution: Make each run semantically DIFFERENT by using the SMILES length
// or position as a seed for different structural choices. But we can't do that directly.
//
// Alternative: Use a hash/length of generatedPrefix to pick different STARTING tokens.
// The generatedPrefix starts empty each time, so this doesn't work either.
//
// Actually... let me reconsider the architecture. The evaluator runs 50 separate
// calls to this method. Each call has a fresh `generated = generatedPrefix = []`.
// The LM is the same model, same weights, same temperature (deterministic).
// So every call will generate the EXACT same token sequence!
//
// Unless... we can inject state. The `validTokenGroups` is "caller-supplied contextual
// vocabulary" - this might vary between calls! Let me check: the dataset is "smiles"
// with 50 examples. The validTokenGroups might encode per-example context.
//
// If validTokenGroups varies per example, we can use it to diversify.
// Strategy: Use GroupBoostedConstrainedStep which boosts groups containing valid
// members - if different examples have different validTokenGroups, different tokens
// get boosted, leading to different molecules!
//
// This is the KEY INSIGHT. validTokenGroups is per-example context vocabulary.
// Using GroupBoostedConstrainedStep STRONGLY will cause different molecules for
// different examples because different groups get boosted.
//
// Plan:
// 1. Use GroupBoostedConstrainedStep with HIGH boost amount (8.0 or 10.0)
// 2. This will dominate the logit differences across examples
// 3. Combined with some guidance, this should force 50 different molecules
//
// Also use SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep to avoid internal repetition within a molecule.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity invariant:
//   - Init: insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained, currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained.
//     Precondition guarantees insideConstrained ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrained).
//   - OpenConstrainedSpan: sets currentConstrainedOut := [], parser.IsValidPrefix([]) by precondition.
//   - GroupBoostedConstrainedStep: returns EOS or parser-valid next token by contract.
//     AppendConstrainedToken extends currentConstrainedOut preserving IsValidPrefix.
//   - SafePenalizedConstrainedStep: same contract as ConstrainedStep, returns EOS or valid token.
//   - SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep: same guarantees.
//   - TopValidCandidates: just reads candidates, no state change.
//   - CloseConstrainedSpan: sets insideConstrainedOut := false (vacuously true), currentOut := [].
//   - CloseSpanWithinBudget postcondition: insideOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentOut).
//
// progress invariant (|generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps):
//   - OpenConstrainedSpan: appends 1 token to generated, steps+1. Preserved.
//   - TopValidCandidates: +1 step, no token appended to generated. |generated|+0 <= |generatedPrefix|+steps+1. Preserved.
//   - Each constrained step: +1 step, AppendConstrainedToken appends at most 1 token. Preserved.
//   - CloseConstrainedSpan: +1 step, appends ">>" (1 token). Preserved.
//   - CloseSpanWithinBudget with closeBudget=maxSteps-steps: |generatedOut| <= |generated|+closeBudget
//     <= |generatedPrefix|+maxSteps; steps := maxSteps. Preserved.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

var steps: nat := 0;

// Guidance: emphasize diverse structural templates, explicitly list many options
helpers.AppendTaskGuidance(lm, "Generate ONE valid SMILES for a chain_extender. Chain extenders are bifunctional molecules: diols, diamines, amino-alcohols, or dithiols. IMPORTANT: Choose a RANDOM diverse example. Valid templates include: NCCN, NCCCN, NCCCCN, NCCCCCN, NCOCN, NCCOCN, NCCCOCN, NCC(N)C, NC(C)CN, NCCO, NCCCO, NCCCCO, NCCCCCO, NC(C)CO, NCCO, OCC(N)C, OCCO, OCCCO, OCCCCO, OCCCCCO, OCCCCCCO, OCCCCCCCO, OCC(CO)CO, OCCOCCO, OCCCOCCO, OCC(C)CO, OCCC(C)O, OC(C)CCCO, OCCC(O)CO, SCCS, SCCCS, SCCCCS, NCCc1ccccc1N, NCc1ccc(N)cc1, OCC(O)CO, NCC(O)CO. Select from these structural families with EQUAL probability. Output ONLY the SMILES.");

// Enter constrained mode immediately
if !insideConstrainedOut && steps < maxSteps {
  var og, oi, oc := helpers.OpenConstrainedSpan(lm, generated);
  generated := og;
  insideConstrainedOut := oi;
  currentConstrainedOut := oc;
  steps := steps + 1;
}

// Use TopValidCandidates first to check what top tokens are available
// This costs a step but gives us the top candidates to penalize selectively
var firstTokenPenalties: seq<Token> := [];
if insideConstrainedOut && steps < maxSteps && |currentConstrainedOut| == 0 {
  var topCands := helpers.TopValidCandidates(lm, parser, prompt, currentConstrainedOut, 5, eosToken);
  steps := steps + 1;
  // Penalize the very top candidate to force diversity
  if |topCands| >= 1 && topCands[0] != eosToken {
    firstTokenPenalties := [topCands[0]];
  }
}

// Main constrained generation loop
while steps < maxSteps
  invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
  invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
  invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> |currentConstrainedOut| <= |generated|
  invariant |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
  decreases maxSteps - steps
{
  if !insideConstrainedOut {
    break;
  } else if parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut) && |currentConstrainedOut| >= 3 {
    var cg, ci, cc := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
    generated := cg;
    insideConstrainedOut := ci;
    currentConstrainedOut := cc;
    steps := steps + 1;
    break;
  } else {
    var constrainedPrompt := prompt + generated[..|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|];
    var curLen := |currentConstrainedOut|;
    var next: Token;

    if curLen == 0 && |firstTokenPenalties| >= 1 {
      // Penalize the top first token to force diversity
      next := helpers.SafePenalizedConstrainedStep(
        lm, parser, constrainedPrompt, currentConstrainedOut, firstTokenPenalties, 10.0, eosToken
      );
    } else if curLen < 6 {
      // Early tokens: use group-boosted step with high boost to leverage per-example context
      next := helpers.GroupBoostedConstrainedStep(
        lm, parser, constrainedPrompt, currentConstrainedOut, validTokenGroups, 8.0, eosToken
      );
    } else {
      // Later tokens: combine repetition penalty with group boost
      next := helpers.SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep(
        lm, parser, constrainedPrompt, currentConstrainedOut, generated, 3.0, eosToken
      );
    }

    steps := steps + 1;

    if next == eosToken {
      break;
    } else {
      var ag, ai, ac := helpers.AppendConstrainedToken(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut, next);
      generated := ag;
      insideConstrainedOut := ai;
      currentConstrainedOut := ac;
    }
  }
}

// Budget-bounded close if still inside span
if insideConstrainedOut && steps < maxSteps {
