// - The problem is pure degeneracy: same molecule generated 50 times
// - "Samples to 100 unique valid (cap 1000): 1000" - even 1000 samples gives <100 unique
//
// Root cause analysis:
// The 50 examples are evaluated with the SAME prompt structure, and the LM+CSD
// always converges to the SAME molecule. The CSD is doing hard parser-constrained
// decoding which is effectively argmax (greedy), producing the same output every time.
//
// What we need: 50 DIFFERENT valid chain extender SMILES from 50 calls.
//
// Key observation from diagnostics:
// - "Applied penalty: 1.9%" in attempt 10 vs "38.9%" in attempt 2
//   Attempt 2 had HIGHER penalty application and HIGHER accuracy (4%)!
