// 
// KEY INSIGHT from rollouts:
// - "NH" = ammonia, not a chain extender (not bifunctional)
// - "OCCO" = ethylene glycol - this IS a valid chain extender but might be an exemplar
// - "CC(O)CC" = 2-butanol - NOT bifunctional (only one OH), not a chain extender
//
// ROOT CAUSE: The minimum length of 4 is too short. Need:
// 1. LONGER minimum length (at least 6-8 chars) to ensure bifunctionality
// 2. Better guidance that emphasizes BIFUNCTIONALITY explicitly
// 3. Possibly check for presence of two functional groups
//
// SPECIFIC PROBLEM WITH TINY SPANS:
// The parser.IsCompletePrefix check at length >= 4 allows:
// - "OCCO" (4 chars) = ethylene glycol (might be exemplar)
// - "NCCN" (4 chars) = ethylenediamine (might be exemplar)
// - "NH" closes at length 2 (below our threshold... but wait, threshold is >= 4)
// - Wait: "NH" is only 2 tokens: "N" and "H" -> length 2 < 4, shouldn't close
// - But the output shows "NH" as extracted... this means the span has "NH" with length 2
// - This means the CloseSpanWithinBudget at the end is closing it with tiny span!
//
// The CloseSpanWithinBudget at the end doesn't check length! It finds ANY complete prefix
// (including "N" if parser.IsCompletePrefix(["N"]) is true). So "N", "NH" etc. could
// be closed by CloseSpanWithinBudget.
//
// FIX: Increase minimum length from 4 to 8 in the CloseConstrainedSpan check,
// AND remove the CloseSpanWithinBudget fallback (or add length check there too).
// OR use a different approach: generate a full chain extender then close.
//
// BETTER APPROACH: 
// 1. Force minimum length of 8 before closing
// 2. Use SafeSoftConstrainedStep throughout (not just first 6) for diversity
// 3. Don't use CloseSpanWithinBudget (it ignores length)
// 4. Use CloseSpanIfComplete but only when length >= 8
// 5. If we run out of budget, use CloseSpanWithinBudget but add safeguard
//
// INSIGHT on diversity: 16/50 unique molecules is good diversity. The problem
// is membership (in-class check). Need more molecules to be truly bifunctional.
//
// REVISED STRATEGY:
// 1. Guidance: explicitly say "minimum 6 heavy atoms, must have exactly two
//    functional groups (OH, NH2, or COOH)"
// 2. Minimum length: 8 tokens before closing
// 3. SafeSoftConstrainedStep for first 10 tokens (diversify early choices)
// 4. SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep for rest
// 5. Close only when length >= 8 AND parser.IsCompletePrefix
// 6. Final CloseSpanWithinBudget still needed for correctness guarantees
//    but we've already ensured length >= 8 by the time we reach it
//    Actually CloseSpanWithinBudget tracks completion and will close at first complete point
//    which might be short... 
// 7. Skip CloseSpanWithinBudget and let the main loop run to budget
